            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Max Born's Early Life</strong><br>\nMax Born was born on December 11, 1882, in Breslau, which was then part of the German Empire. He showed an early talent in mathematics, which led him to study the subject along with physics at the Universities of Breslau, Heidelberg, and Zurich. Born had a passion for understanding the underlying principles of the physical world, which drove him to delve deeper into academic research and made significant contributions to the field of quantum mechanics.</p>\n\n<p><strong>University Contributions</strong><br>\nAfter completing his education, Max Born held various professorial positions at universities across Germany. He worked at the University of Berlin, and later at the University of Göttingen, where he became one of the foremost researchers in quantum mechanics. His work during this time helped lay the groundwork for future scientific discoveries and cemented his reputation as a leading thinker in physics and mathematics.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Quantum Mechanics and Physics</strong><br>\nMax Born is best known for his work in formulating the quantum theory, which revolutionizes our understanding of atomic and subatomic processes. In 1926, he proposed the probability interpretation of the wave function, a fundamental principle in the theory of quantum mechanics, for which he would later receive the Nobel Prize in Physics in 1954.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
